{% comment %}
  FUEL_09 preview switch. Rendered once from the head of layout/theme.liquid.

  The offer box on the product page (snippets/fuel09-box.liquid) ships
  hidden and is opened by a class on <html>: ab-f09-v1 for look A, ab-f09-v2
  for look B, ab-f09-v3 for look C. In production only the testing tool adds
  that class. This switch is for QA on a theme that is not the live one:
  #f09-v1, #f09-v2 or #f09-v3 in the address turns that look on, #f09-off
  turns them all off. The choice is kept
  in sessionStorage, so it survives clicking through the site like a customer
  instead of retyping the hash on every page.

  The whole script is left out of the live theme in Liquid (theme.role is
  'main' there), so none of this can ever run for a shopper.

  A hash that names a look also takes the other looks off, because no two
  are ever meant to be on together. Replaying the stored choice only ever
  adds: the testing tool's own preview runs on these themes too, and an
  ordinary fragment jump (the skip to content link is the first focusable
  element on every page) must not take its class away. #f09-off is the one
  explicit way back out.

  It runs in the head, before the body is parsed, so the look is already on
  when the box and the size tiles are laid out.
{% endcomment %}
{%- if theme.role != 'main' -%}
  <script>
    (() => {
      const root = document.documentElement;
      const looks = { '#f09-v1': 'ab-f09-v1', '#f09-v2': 'ab-f09-v2', '#f09-v3': 'ab-f09-v3' };
      const classes = Object.values(looks);

      const apply = () => {
        const { hash } = window.location;
        const off = hash === '#f09-off';
        const asked = looks[hash] ?? null;
        let look = asked;
        try {
          if (asked) sessionStorage.setItem('fuel09Qa', asked);
          if (off) sessionStorage.removeItem('fuel09Qa');
          if (!look) look = sessionStorage.getItem('fuel09Qa');
        } catch (error) {
          // Storage can be blocked; the hash alone still works for that load.
        }

        if (off) {
          root.classList.remove(...classes);
        } else if (classes.includes(look)) {
          if (asked) root.classList.remove(...classes);
          root.classList.add(look);
        }
      };

      apply();
      window.addEventListener('hashchange', apply);
    })();
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{% comment %}
  FUEL_09 mystery bottle, after it is in the cart. On every theme and every
  page, the live one included: the bottle goes into the cart on the product
  page (assets/fuel09-offer.js) and has to stay right in the cart drawer and
  on the cart page wherever the shopper goes next.

  The bottle is an ordinary product with a price. What makes it free is a
  discount code of the client's gift app, which accepts the code only on a
  cart carrying the attribute _fuel09=on and with enough sale bottles in it.
  The box writes a second attribute, _fuel09_gift ("item:code"), and that is
  all this script reads: no setting, no class on <html>. A cart without it
  costs nothing here, not even a request, because Liquid prints below whether
  the attribute is there.

  What it does once the cart has come to rest:

  - the code or the mark is gone (other apps on this store rewrite the code
    list): both are put back, other codes kept;
  - a bottle is still not free on a second look, with code and mark in place
    (the shopper went below the bottles the offer asks for, or holds more
    bottles than the offer frees): those bottles are taken out, so nobody
    pays for a gift;
  - no bottle left, on a second look as well: the code and both marks come
    off.

  It never puts a bottle in.

  Timing. After every change several apps write to this cart for seconds on
  end (the price testing app sends each line again, more than once; the gift
  app adds its own gifts and attributes), and a cart read in the middle of
  that is not the cart the shopper ends up with. So nothing is decided until
  no cart write of anyone's has finished for a second and a half. The
  browser's own list of finished requests says so (PerformanceObserver), for
  fetch, XMLHttpRequest and sendBeacon alike, with nothing of the page
  wrapped or replaced. The observer only exists while a cart carries the
  attribute. While the box is adding (between its two events, fuel09:adding
  and fuel09:gift) the script stands back altogether: the marks are on the
  cart then and the bottle is not there yet.

  Each write is followed by the theme's own cart update word, so the drawer
  and the cart page redraw themselves. Putting the same code back a third
  time within ten seconds is skipped, so this cannot loop with an app that
  keeps writing its own list.
{% endcomment %}
<script>
  (() => {
    const MARK = '_fuel09';
    const GIFT = '_fuel09_gift';
    const OWN = 'fuel09-gift';
    const FLAG = 'fuel09Gift';
    const QUIET = 1500;
    const WRITES = /\/cart\/(add|change|update|clear)(\.js|\.json)?(\?|$)/;
    const cartUrl = `${ {{ routes.cart_url | json }} }.js`;
    const updateUrl = `${ {{ routes.cart_update_url | json }} }.js`;

    const flag = (value) => {
      try {
        if (value === undefined) return sessionStorage.getItem(FLAG) === '1';
        if (value) sessionStorage.setItem(FLAG, '1');
        else sessionStorage.removeItem(FLAG);
      } catch (error) {
        // Storage can be blocked; Liquid's reading below still arms the page.
      }
      return false;
    };

    let timer = 0;
    let watcher = null;
    let busy = false;
    let again = false;
    let hold = false;
    let doubt = '';
    let failures = 0;
    let restores = [];

    const later = (wait = QUIET) => {
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = window.setTimeout(check, wait);
    };
    // Any cart write that finishes, whoever sent it, starts the wait again.
    const arm = () => {
      flag(true);
      if (!watcher && 'PerformanceObserver' in window) {
        watcher = new PerformanceObserver((list) => {
          if (list.getEntries().some((entry) => WRITES.test(entry.name))) later();
        });
        watcher.observe({ type: 'resource' });
      }
      later();
    };
    const disarm = () => {
      flag(false);
      watcher?.disconnect();
      watcher = null;
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      doubt = '';
    };

    const read = async () => {
      const response = await fetch(cartUrl, { cache: 'no-store', headers: { Accept: 'application/json' } });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`cart ${response.status}`);
      return response.json();
    };
    const write = async (body) => {
      const response = await fetch(updateUrl, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ ...body, sections: 'cart-icon-bubble', sections_url: window.location.pathname })
      });
      if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`cart ${response.status}`);
      const state = await response.json();
      const bubble = document.getElementById('cart-icon-bubble');
      const html = state.sections?.['cart-icon-bubble'];
      const fresh = html ? new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html').querySelector('.shopify-section') : null;
      if (bubble && fresh) bubble.innerHTML = fresh.innerHTML;
      if (typeof publish === 'function' && typeof PUB_SUB_EVENTS === 'object') {
        publish(PUB_SUB_EVENTS.cartUpdate, { source: OWN, cartData: state });
      }
    };

    // How many bottles of a line the code has made free.
    const freed = (item) => {
      if (!item.original_price) return item.quantity;
      const off = item.original_line_price - item.final_line_price;
      return Math.min(item.quantity, Math.floor(off / item.original_price + 0.001));
    };
    // A finding counts on the second look in a row that makes it, and the
    // second look comes only after the cart has been at rest once more.
    const twice = (finding) => {
      if (doubt === finding) {
        doubt = '';
        return true;
      }
      doubt = finding;
      later();
      return false;
    };

    const check = async () => {
      // The box is in the middle of adding. It says when it is through.
      if (hold) return;
      if (busy) {
        again = true;
        return;
      }
      busy = true;
      try {
        const cart = await read();
        const attributes = cart.attributes ?? {};
        const [id, code] = String(attributes[GIFT] ?? '').split(':');
        if (!id || !code) {
          disarm();
          return;
        }
        const bottles = (cart.items ?? []).filter((item) => String(item.variant_id) === id);
        const codes = (cart.discount_codes ?? []).map((entry) => String(entry.code));
        const others = codes.filter((other) => other.toLowerCase() !== code.toLowerCase());
        const listed = others.length < codes.length;

        if (!bottles.length) {
          if (!twice('gone')) return;
          await write({ discount: others.join(','), attributes: { [MARK]: '', [GIFT]: '' } });
          disarm();
          return;
        }
        if (!listed || attributes[MARK] !== 'on') {
          doubt = '';
          const now = Date.now();
          restores = restores.filter((time) => now - time < 10000);
          if (restores.length >= 2) return;
          restores.push(now);
          await write({ discount: [...others, code].join(','), attributes: { [MARK]: 'on' } });
          return;
        }
        if (bottles.every((item) => freed(item) >= item.quantity)) {
          doubt = '';
          failures = 0;
          return;
        }
        if (!twice('paid')) return;
        // By item where it is one line: the price testing app gives a line
        // a new key each time it sends it again.
        const updates = {};
        if (bottles.length === 1) updates[id] = freed(bottles[0]);
        else for (const item of bottles) updates[item.key] = freed(item);
        await write({ updates });
        failures = 0;
      } catch (error) {
        // A write the cart refused (a line key gone stale under another
        // app's write) is tried again on a fresh read, three times at most.
        failures += 1;
        if (failures < 3) later();
      } finally {
        busy = false;
        if (again) {
          again = false;
          later();
        }
      }
    };

    document.addEventListener('fuel09:adding', () => {
      hold = true;
    });
    document.addEventListener('fuel09:gift', () => {
      hold = false;
      arm();
    });
    if ({{ cart.attributes['_fuel09_gift'] | default: '' | json }} !== '' || flag()) {
      if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', arm);
      else arm();
    }
  })();
</script>
